# Copilot Instructions — {{project.name}}

> Workspace-level instructions for GitHub Copilot and Claude.

## Entry Point

Read `openspec/AGENTS.md` first. It contains the full project configuration, architecture rules, and code placement guidelines.

## Agentic Workflow

This project uses a three-layer agentic workflow: **Agent → Command → Skill**.

| Layer | Location | Invoked As | Purpose |
|-------|----------|------------|---------|
| **Agents** | `.github/agents/` | `@agent-name` in Copilot chat | Enforce behavioral rules, guide interaction |
| **Commands** | `.github/prompts/` | `/command-name` in chat | Structured invocation, parameterized execution |
| **Skills** | `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/` | Referenced by commands | Detailed step-by-step workflow execution |

### Available Workflows

| Command | Agent | Skill | Purpose |
|---------|-------|-------|---------|
| `/discover` | `@discover` | `discovery.md` | Explore and shape ideas before planning |
| `/plan` | `@plan` | `planning.md` | Create DDD-compliant proposals |
| `/implement` | `@implement` | `implementation.md` | Execute approved proposals inside-out |
| `/troubleshoot` | `@troubleshoot` | `troubleshooting.md` | Diagnose bugs and architecture violations |

### Execution Chain

1. **Agent** receives user request and enforces hard rules (no code in discovery, proposal required for implementation, etc.)
2. **Agent** loads the corresponding **Command** from `.github/prompts/`
3. **Command** references the **Skill** in `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/`
4. **Skill** defines the step-by-step execution, context loading, and output format

### Direct Command Use

Commands can be invoked directly as `/discover`, `/plan`, `/implement`, `/troubleshoot` without going through an agent. The agent adds behavioral guardrails and interaction style on top.

## Architecture Rules

- **DDD + Onion Architecture + CQRS** — see `openspec/specs/architecture/`
- Dependencies point inward: Domain ← Application ← Infrastructure ← Presentation
- Domain layer has ZERO external dependencies
- One repository per aggregate root
- Cross-context communication via integration events only

## Approved AI Tools

Only GitHub Copilot, Claude, and Codex. No agent frameworks (LangChain, AutoGen, CrewAI, Semantic Kernel). See `openspec/specs/architecture/agent-limits.md`.
